    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (66.51) and **Taylor Ward** (64.16) anchor our lineup as the premier plays. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Germ\u00e1n M\u00e1rquez, whose 5.64 xERA provides a significant cushion for production; batting in the #2 hole ensures maximum plate appearances against a weak arm. While **Taylor Ward** faces the weather risk inherent in the Matthew Boyd matchup, his platoon advantage and favorable park factors make him a high-floor start. Similarly, **Gavin Sheets** (63.22) earns a strong rating by successfully navigating the tough Zac Gallen matchup, boosted by a favorable batting order position that compensates for the SP\u2019s high skill level.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involves our outfield and corner infield configuration, particularly regarding the benching of **Jung Hoo Lee** (46.14). While **Jung Hoo Lee** graded well against Spencer Miles, he was narrowly edged by **Tyler Freeman** (60.18), whose combination of neutral platoon splits and stolen base potential\u2014supported by a slow opposing pitcher delivery\u2014makes him the more efficient option for our 5x5 constraints. We are also monitoring the rain risk (44%) in the matchup against Matthew Boyd, which directly impacts **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Dylan Beavers**, and **Taylor Ward**. Should that game be postponed, we will need to pivot quickly to **Lawrence Butler** or **Drew Gilbert** from the bench to ensure we don't bleed categorical production. \n\nBeyond these risks, **Jonathan Aranda** (56.29) remains a high-value play today; despite Will Warren\u2019s decent xERA, **Jonathan Aranda** maintains an elite platoon-driven score that makes him a lock at 1B. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Bryson Stott** (55.60) and **Daulton Varsho** (55.64). **Daulton Varsho** is particularly interesting as his stolen base upside is boosted by the opponent's slow delivery speed, keeping his efficiency high despite a difficult matchup against Trevor McDonald. As we move closer to lock, we will monitor official lineups for **Yainer Diaz**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, and the rest of our active squad to ensure the projected batting positions hold firm.",
